  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of JIAF Project Management Unit (PMU) for the Implementation of the Joint Inter-Sectoral Analysis Framework 2021-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Joint Intersectoral Analysis Group (JIAG) was formed mid-2017 to develop an approach to analyse the needs of crisis-affected people in a joint, comprehensive, and methodologically sound manner in line with Grand Bargain commitments. The specific objective was to produce a Joint Intersectoral Analysis Framework (JIAF) that will enable to analyse the various dimensions of a crisis (context, impact) and its underlying factors, as well as the resulting effects on people&#x2019;s lives and livelihoods combining multiple sectors and their interactions. This project provides additional, required cost coverage to ensure the recruitment of the Project Manager (JIAF) for a full one-year period, in order to effectively and successfully finalize all tasks.</narrative>
  </description>
